        "id": 1649662
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T07:10:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we remove these lines? With the current patch, ARC still fails this test because we fail `ensureWifiConnected`. I think the current patch only runs after this point? \n\nWith these lines removed, I checked that ARC and raven both pass with this patch",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2791,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2796,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d6cfe744a1b086d2df5c659fc5ecb00f7adb2314",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4e33f999_91db7589",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T07:20:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "preparePartialConnectivity sets the validation URLs to some test URLs, so wifi does need to be restarted to restore normal behavior.\n\nWhy does ARC fail at this point ? If this is a behavior difference in ARC and not a test error, it sounds like the ARC behavior should be fixed. I see some special casing is being introduced during CTS runs (ag/19286988), which does not seem like the expected device behavior in general.",
      "parentUuid": "93cf8713_757b89e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2791,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2796,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d6cfe744a1b086d2df5c659fc5ecb00f7adb2314",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7dc90c4a_f04e6c20",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1649662
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T07:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why does ARC fail at this point ?\nARC fails at this point because during ensureWifiConnected, it grabs the current `connectionInfo` (http://cs/android/frameworks/libs/net/common/testutils/devicetests/com/android/testutils/ConnectUtil.kt;l\u003d65;rcl\u003d958fa6aaac50007572970f8a3047c366252f2b93). Since ARC hasn\u0027t fully disabled its network yet, the connectionInfo will be the about-to-be-disconnected, non-null object. It then skips the `if` block on line 66 and waits for an onAvailable to be called on the test callback. Meanwhile on the ARC side, we\u0027re now processing a disable event and we end up in a disabled state with no trigger to re-enable wifi. So `ConnectUtil` will wait until the timeout and see no new onAvailabe and fail.\n\n\n\u003e  see some special casing is being introduced during CTS runs (ag/19286988)\nThe special casing is because we don\u0027t actually support Android captive portals in ARC. So we only pretend to enable it during CTS tests so the tests can run and pass. We could special case passing this test in ARC as well, but it would look something like purposely blocking for 3 seconds in `handleSetWifiEnabled(false)` so that by the time `ensureWifiConnected` runs here, the network is fully disabled. If possible, we\u0027d like to avoid that kind of behavior since that\u0027ll affect all wifi state changes in ARC, not just during CTS tests.",
      "parentUuid": "4e33f999_91db7589",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2791,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2796,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d6cfe744a1b086d2df5c659fc5ecb00f7adb2314",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ec026926_af70e598",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1649662
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T07:37:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding was that disabling wifi is an asynchronous event and that this test doesn\u0027t have a way to wait/check for a network to be fully disabled before proceeding with ensureWifiConnected - although I may be missing something here?\n\nI think the root issue is that depending on how long it takes for wifi to finish disabling, ensureWifiConnected might or might not read the correct `connectionInfo` object?",
      "parentUuid": "7dc90c4a_f04e6c20",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2791,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2796,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d6cfe744a1b086d2df5c659fc5ecb00f7adb2314",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9ab25c02_efe2cdad",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1304263
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-02T08:08:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wifi network should be torn down after l.2788. (The svc command in l.2794 should only turn the wifi off, not relying on the command to disconnect wifi) If we did not reconnect the WiFi, I expect ARC will have no working internet which should fail in tearDown() if you remove the ensureWifiConnected. Is the WiFi network in ARC not  disconnected? It should not be the case. Otherwise, test should fail while waiting for the onLost in l.2788.",
      "parentUuid": "93cf8713_757b89e7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2791,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2796,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d6cfe744a1b086d2df5c659fc5ecb00f7adb2314",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af399052_1aa2c3e7",
        "filename": "tests/cts/net/src/android/net/cts/ConnectivityManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 2796,
      "author": {
        "id": 1649662
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-08-03T01:15:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah I see. ARC does see an onLost callback on l.2788 (the onLost looks like it\u0027s triggered within the Connectivity stack). But ARC\u0027s wifi stack doesn\u0027t reset the `connInfo` until after we receive a callback from the host saying it\u0027s fully disconnected (which happens a few seconds later).\n\nI\u0027ll take a look at this in the meantime, but this is starting to look like an ARC-specific change. Thanks for all the help!",
      "parentUuid": "9ab25c02_efe2cdad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2791,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 2796,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "d6cfe744a1b086d2df5c659fc5ecb00f7adb2314",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
